// user/ci/hdesk.ci: the hybrid desk on the keyboard (H-3a, docs/specs/2026-11-05-h-hybrid.md sections 4 to 7).
//   hdesk
// on the framebuffer only: becomes the tiler (FBIO_TILER) and runs desktops 1..9 under a 28 px bar (K-5). A window is a
// terminal (user/ci/terms.ci on a pty whose slave is /sh's 0, 1 and 2) or a pixel client (a process that opened
// /dev/fb0 and took the tile set next, told by FBIO_TILE_SYNC 4 and named by FBIO_TILE_INFO). The desk boots with
// one terminal filling the plane (HX-7). user/ci/kit/layout.ci lays the active desktop out and cuts each window's
// visible rectangles; the desk paints the plane a row at a time, bottom window first (2 px ultramarine border on the
// focused window, 1 px ink at rest, a nested 1 px sienna or ochre ring on a window whose foreground holds the disk or
// network grant, terminals' cells, paper), and places each pixel client with FBIO_TILE_PLACE at
// the largest integer scale that fits its content box, centered (HX-4), its rectangles the visible ones within the
// scaled surface. Chords with Super: Enter a new terminal, q SIGTERM to the focused window's foreground process,
// Shift+q Shut Down and Shift+r Restart (each pressed twice within 2 s, FF-R6 B),
// arrows the focus, 1..9 a desktop, Shift+1..9 the focused window there, f float, z monocle, m minimize, Shift+m
// restore. Alt+Tab, Alt+Shift+Tab and Super+Tab open the switcher (HX-11): the active desktop's windows most recent
// first, the second selected; Tab and the arrows move; releasing the key that opened it chooses; Esc closes.
// DN-6 frame 10: the switcher is a plate of radius 16 centered on the plane, one row of 116 px tiles (the window's
// icon and name, the selected tile FILL), as many as the screen holds; Up and Down go to the first and the last.
// K-6 (docs/specs/2026-11-07-k-kit2.md): the bar's clock at its right, `Www Mmm D  HH:MM` from the kernel's date
// (FBIO_TILE_INFO kind 2: live when the boot read one, A-3, else the fixed epoch 2026-01-01 00:00), turned by
// FBIO_TILE_SYNC 5; Super+c or a click on the clock opens the calendar under it, the month of today with today's cell in
// ultramarine; Left and Right step the month, Esc closes; every other key goes where it went with the calendar shut.
// Arguments: `--run TEXT` types TEXT and Enter into the first terminal at boot; `--monocle` opens the first pixel
// window in monocle (G-5's play run: doom straight into a window).
// Lines for tools/check-hdesk.py: `hdesk: layout` and `hdesk: win` at each layout, `hdesk: place`, `hdesk: bar`,
// `hdesk: switcher`, `hdesk: clock |TEXT|` when the clock's text changes, `hdesk: calendar YYYY-MM first W days N today D`
// at each month the calendar shows, `hdesk: grant i G` when a window's grant word changes, `hdesk: grant list G open`;
// when the first terminal's shell ends, its bytes, rows (UTF-8, each cell's code point as drawn) and cursor, and the
// desk ends.
// K-5 (E2-1, KD-1 A): the bar is 28 px: the mark (AA-1: the Albers d roundel, user/ci/kit/roundel.ci; a click opens the Super plane), the App
// pill (the focused window's title and `v`; a click opens its dropdown) and its variable, the desktops 1..9 as pills
// (the active filled, an occupied one framed, a 4 x 4 pip in a grant's color), the grant pills `DISK n` and `NET n`
// (the windows holding each; a click lists them, title, pid and desktop, KD-1 A: law 4 names them one click from the
// bar) and the clock. `hdesk: bar desktop D |TITLE| var |VARIABLE| grants |PILLS|` when any of it changes.
// K-7 (E2-3, KD-2 B): tiles sit GAP (8 px at 1x) apart and from the plane's edges (layout.ci), and the color mark is
// the plane's emblem, centered, 480 px a side portrait and 440 landscape at 1x, under every window.
// WB-1 (docs/specs/2026-11-07-wb-window-bars.md): a float has a bar inside its border, its title and variable and
// four buttons at the right, minimize, fullscreen, tile, close; its content box is the frame less the bar. WB-5
// (the design's table), DN-6 and DN-23: the bar is 32 px at 1x, the buttons 24 px stroked glyphs
// (kit/wbglyph.ci), no gap; a focused window's outline and bar take its ring's color (ring 3 ultramarine, a net grant's ring 2 sienna, a
// disk grant's ring 1 ochre), a window at rest a rule border, its grant's ring nested, and a neutral bar. A left press on the bar and a drag moves the float; a press
// and release on one button acts (`hdesk: bar button K window I`); a second press on the bar within 500 ms of a still
// click is fullscreen (`hdesk: bar double I`). F11 is Super+z unless a pixel client holds the grab (WB-R2 A); a
// second press gives the window back the mode it had (`hdesk: fullscreen I on` and `off`). WB-4 (WB-R4 A): the close
// button ends every process of the window, a terminal's whole session (`hdesk: close I (status)`).
// FF-5 (docs/specs/2026-11-07-ff-super-plane.md sections 3 and 3c): a clean Super tap or a click on the mark opens
// the Super plane in place of the Super menu (user/ci/kit/plane.ci, agy's desk edition 3): the field, pinned, recent
// files, the machine (desktops, grants, the month, the windows by desktop), the matches and the preview, the
// actions. Typing filters every window, Settings, /bin's programs and the files of /home (the index of FF-1, its
// ring /dev/fsidx read when the plane opens); Enter opens the selected row (a window focused and restored, a program
// in a new terminal, a file by the open table of FF-3, a directory into the field); Tab the preview; Super+p pins;
// Esc, a second tap or a click on the margin closes; any other chord closes it and acts. Super+, opens Settings.
// Lines: `hdesk: ff open ...`, `hdesk: ff |QUERY| rows N sel S` and a `hdesk: ff row` line a row, `hdesk: ff chose`,
// `hdesk: ff action A`, `hdesk: ff closed`.
